# spelling.help

spelling.help is a web app to practice spelling for a competition with a customizable word list.

spellingdrills.pages.dev

- text to speech
- speech to letters
- NATO alphabet
- progress tracking system

## History

### Problem

In my school we were told we would have a spelling bee competition on August 11th. I had a week of preparation, so I started practicing every day with the list of words the teacher handed out, memorizing all of them, but when I wanted to test my knowledge with a pronouncer, no one had time to speak all the words. I noticed a problem on August 7th:

Competitors might not have a pronouncer to test their knowledge, and other apps' word lists aren't customizable or the web app isn't free.

spelling.help solves all these problems.

### Constraints

With only four days, I used Claude Code to generate the code while I orchestrated the structure of the project.

### Outcome

The outcome was a web app that had the tools any speller would need: text to speech, speech to letters, NATO alphabet, and a progress tracking system.

After two days of development, I drilled with it from August 9 to 10, providing me with a better knowledge of the words. On August 11th I won first place in the Spelling Bee Competition.
